From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: revenant <revenant@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Truncate in-range doubles to int32 in VFP registers on armv7

The fast path of _sh_ljs_tryfast_truncate_to_int32, which ToInt32, the bitwise operators and the
shifts use, converted with vcvt, moved the result from s0 to a core register and back, converted
it to a double again and compared with vcmp and vmrs. On the Cortex-A9 of the iPhone 4S the moves
between the core and VFP registers and the flags transfer of vmrs stall the pipeline, and every
ToInt32 paid for them.

The round trip is only there to reject the values that do not truncate to ToInt32. A number with
|x| below 2^31 truncates to ToInt32(x) whether or not it is an integer, since vcvt truncates toward
zero, so the fast path now accepts all of them and sends the rest to the slow path as before.

The range is decided by the high word alone: |x| is below 2^31 when the masked high word is below
0x41e00000. NaN, infinity and every tagged value fail that test. The new helper
_sh_ljs_tryfast_truncate_to_int32_at reads the value from memory, converts it with vcvt.s32.f64 and
vcvt.f64.s32 in VFP registers, and returns the truncated number as a double, which ToInt32 stores
as it is. No operand passes through the core registers. Other platforms keep the previous helper,
behind the same portable name.
---
diff --git a/include/hermes/VM/sh_legacy_value.h b/include/hermes/VM/sh_legacy_value.h
--- a/include/hermes/VM/sh_legacy_value.h
+++ b/include/hermes/VM/sh_legacy_value.h
@@ -340,6 +340,18 @@
   return true;
 #endif
 
+#if defined(__GNUC__) && defined(__ARM_ARCH_7A__) && defined(__VFP_FP__)
+  // The high word decides the range without a floating-point compare: |v| is
+  // below 2^31 exactly when its masked high word is below 0x41e00000. NaN and
+  // infinity are above it, and every tagged value has a high word from
+  // 0xf9000000 up, which is above it once the sign is cleared. Inside the range
+  // vcvt truncates toward zero, which is ToInt32 for integers and fractions
+  // alike, so no round trip is needed.
+  if ((((uint32_t)(v.raw >> 32)) & 0x7fffffffu) >= 0x41e00000u)
+    return false;
+  *res = _sh_tryfast_f64_to_i32_cvt(v.f64);
+  return true;
+#else
   // Since we use NaN-boxing for non-number values, we know that any
   // non-number values will fail the attempted conversion to int32. So we can
   // simply attempt the conversion without checking for numbers.
@@ -351,6 +363,34 @@
     *res = _sh_tryfast_f64_to_i32_cvt(v.f64);
     return (double)*res == v.f64;
   }
+#endif
+}
+
+/// Like _sh_ljs_tryfast_truncate_to_int32, but reads the value from memory and
+/// stores the truncated number as a double, so that on armv7 the value never
+/// passes through the core registers.
+static inline bool _sh_ljs_tryfast_truncate_to_int32_at(
+    const void *value,
+    double *res) {
+#if defined(__GNUC__) && defined(__ARM_ARCH_7A__) && defined(__VFP_FP__) && \
+    !defined(__ARM_FEATURE_JCVT)
+  const uint32_t *words = (const uint32_t *)value;
+  if ((words[1] & 0x7fffffffu) >= 0x41e00000u)
+    return false;
+  float temp;
+  double truncated;
+  asm("vcvt.s32.f64 %0, %P1" : "=t"(temp) : "w"(*(const double *)value));
+  asm("vcvt.f64.s32 %P0, %1" : "=w"(truncated) : "t"(temp));
+  *res = truncated;
+  return true;
+#else
+  SHLegacyValue v = *(const SHLegacyValue *)value;
+  int32_t truncated;
+  if (!_sh_ljs_tryfast_truncate_to_int32(v, &truncated))
+    return false;
+  *res = (double)truncated;
+  return true;
+#endif
 }
 
 /// Test whether the given HermesValues are both non-NaN number values.
diff --git a/lib/VM/Interpreter.cpp b/lib/VM/Interpreter.cpp
index 86a07f19..21a89fb1 100644
--- a/lib/VM/Interpreter.cpp
+++ b/lib/VM/Interpreter.cpp
@@ -2342,11 +2342,11 @@ tailCall:
       }
 
       CASE(ToInt32) {
-        int32_t argInt;
-        if (LLVM_LIKELY(
-                _sh_ljs_tryfast_truncate_to_int32(O2REG(ToInt32), &argInt))) {
+        double truncated;
+        if (LLVM_LIKELY(_sh_ljs_tryfast_truncate_to_int32_at(
+                &O2REG(ToInt32), &truncated))) {
           /* Fast-path. */
-          O1REG(ToInt32) = HermesValue::encodeTrustedNumberValue(argInt);
+          O1REG(ToInt32) = HermesValue::encodeTrustedNumberValue(truncated);
         } else {
           CAPTURE_IP(res = toInt32_RJS(runtime, Handle<>(&O2REG(ToInt32))));
           if (LLVM_UNLIKELY(res == ExecutionStatus::EXCEPTION))
